{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/160746-geist-and-prometheans","id":160746,"title":"Geist and Prometheans","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-06T06:03:23-07:00","id":160746,"title":"Geist and Prometheans","content":"So, one of my favourite bits from the (very very impressive) Blood and Smoke book was a piece of fiction that depicted two Ordo Draculs investigating an old gym that was inhabited by what seems to be a Promethean.<br /> <br /> The way it was written/played, and the way that the Promethean came across as an absolutely alien thing really appeals to me, and I was considering doing something similar in a Geist one shot. <br /> <br /> Problem is, I know NOTHING about Promethean (beyond, y'know, Frankenstein). <br /> <br /> So, advice? How would I go about putting something together like this (no pun intended)? What about the Promethean do I play up, and what do I leave? How do ghosts react to its presence? Does it try to communicate? And how does it defend itself if things go bad? <br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3192-baileyborough","name":"baileyborough","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T03:58:02-07:00","id":161554,"title":"","content":"Prometheans are generally created through either murder or grave robbery, that could come to a sin-eater's attention, some prometheans can heal through a similar method. <br /> <br /> Ulgans can interact with ghosts too.<br /> <br /> Some prometheans study other supernaturals, including the ability to pass as a member of another splat. <br /> <br /> Ulgans can only turn someone's corpse into a promethean if they are touched by the spiritual, so if the sin-eaters know any mortal mediums perhaps upon death they get converted into a new promethean. <br /> <br /> Many promethean lineages have mythic origins, depending on the sin-eater's religious streak that might have a connection, off the top of my head greek myth, egyptian myth, shamanism, babylonian or jewish. So if a sin-eater krewe uses any of those as the basis for their geist's identities that could cause some interesting interactions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T06:17:51-07:00","id":161607,"title":"","content":"I am planning something for my own Geist quest, in which an Ulgan comes to London in an effort to see the worlds largest most sprawling community, in an effort to better understand what drives humen to cling together in cities and groups and whatnot. Over time, this causes all the ghosts to go haywire, and sets the Sin-Eaters on, making them irretated, annoyed and jumpy, because their Geist-Half gets upset by the Ulgans pressence.<br /> This is a pretty good angle I find. Theres been a number of murders around town recently, and the Ulgans pressence will only add to the increasing unrest. It'll be a blast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}